# ========================================
# SamaanShare - Git Ignore Configuration
# Next.js + TypeScript + Prisma + Vercel
# ========================================

# ----------------
# Dependencies
# ----------------
node_modules/
.pnp/
.pnp.js
.yarn/install-state.gz

# ----------------
# Next.js
# ----------------
.next/
out/
build/

# ----------------
# TypeScript
# ----------------
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ----------------
# Testing
# ----------------
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# ----------------
# Prisma
# ----------------
# Generated Prisma Client (auto-generated, don't commit)
# Rebuilt by the postinstall hook / `npm run db:generate`
#
# NOTHING UNDER HERE IS TRACKED, and it must stay that way. Until 18 Aug 2026
# twenty-seven of these files were tracked anyway - added before this rule
# existed, then kept alive by `git add -f` each time a new model appeared. That
# half-tracked state was worse than either alternative: `models.ts` was committed
# while two of the files it re-exports (PasswordResetToken,
# EmailVerificationToken) never were, so a fresh checkout of main carried imports
# pointing at files that were not in the repo.
#
# If you are about to force-add a generated file because something cannot find
# it, run `npm run db:generate` instead - that is the actual fix, and it is what
# postinstall already does on every install.
src/generated/
# Note: schema.prisma and migrations/ SHOULD be committed

# ----------------
# Environment Variables
# ----------------
# Local env files (contain secrets - NEVER commit these)
.env
# Glob rather than the four standard Next suffixes: a `.env.staging.local` was
# created during Stage A6 and slipped past the explicit list into a commit,
# because "staging" is not one of Next's conventional environment names. Any
# *.local env file is by definition machine-local and must never be committed.
.env*.local

# Only .env.example should be committed (no real secrets)
!.env.example

# ----------------
# Vercel
# ----------------
.vercel/

# ----------------
